From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netapi32: the global group None, the group writes, the messenger calls and workstation transports

A computer that is not a domain controller has one global group in its account database, None (relative id 513, Ordinary users), with every account in it -- NetUserGetGroups said so already, NetGroupEnum and NetGroupGetInfo said NERR_InvalidComputer. They now report it at levels 0-3, 1002, 1005 (level 3 with the account domain's SID + 513), and NetGroupGetUsers (a spec stub) lists the accounts, with prefmaxlen/resume. NetGroupAdd, NetGroupDel, NetGroupDelUser, NetGroupSetInfo, NetGroupSetUsers and NetUserSetGroups (spec stubs) check their arguments, the computer and the caller and then say NERR_NotPrimary like NetGroupAddUser (global groups are edited on domain controllers), NERR_GroupNotFound / NERR_GroupExists / NERR_UserNotFound where the name says so. NetMessageBufferSend, NetMessageNameAdd/Del/Enum/GetInfo (spec stubs) return ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED after their checks, as Windows documents since Vista (no messenger service); NetWkstaTransportAdd/Del, documented Not supported, the same after level and administrator checks. All are imported by pywin32's win32net (Anki). lmaccess.h gains GROUP_INFO_*, GROUP_USERS_INFO_* and the prototypes.
